	(lib_symbols)
	(text "ROOT SHEET - BLOCK MAP ONLY, DELIBERATELY UNWIRED (see docs/DECISIONS.md DEC-0009)\n\nEach block below is a hierarchical sheet in its own .kicad_sch file so that follow-up\nworkers can each own exactly one file and never collide (see AGENTS.md).\n\nBoth upstream authorities have now landed and the blocks below are reconciled against\nthem:\n  - docs/FAFF-2-Electronics-Full.svg  - the FAFF 2 electronics block diagram\n  - hardware/cubemx/ARIA_SRB_FAFF_2_POC_CBs_1.ioc - STM32H723VET6, the pin-map authority\n\nSheet pins and root-level wiring are still NOT drawn. A sheet pin only passes ERC once\nthe child sheet declares the matching hierarchical label, and those labels are created\nby the per-block tasks that own each child file. Root wiring is therefore the first\nintegration pass AFTER the blocks are drawn, not part of this skeleton (DEC-0009).\n\nThe interface lists inside each child sheet are the binding contract in the meantime.\nA block worker that needs an interface not listed there must raise it rather than\ninventing it, so two blocks never disagree about a shared net.\n\nNOTE: the block diagram is signal-architecture only - it shows no power blocks. The two\npower sheets below are carried by the specification (REQ-EL-01..04), not the diagram.\n\nLeft-to-right signal flow: power in -> rails -> sensing / MCU -> motor drive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
